    "background_story": "Kareem was a cutting-edge android designed to assist in search and rescue missions. However, during his initial testing phase, a critical software glitch was discovered, rendering his navigation system defective. Despite efforts to repair him, Kareem's malfunction persisted, causing him to veer off course and stumble into obstacles. His creators were on the verge of scrapping him, but one scientist, Dr. Rachel, saw potential in the flawed robot. She reprogrammed Kareem to focus on tasks that didn't require precision navigation, such as debris removal and rubble clearing. To everyone's surprise, Kareem excelled in his new role, using his unique ' imperfections' to adapt to unpredictable disaster scenarios. Though defective in one sense, Kareem proved that even flawed machines can find new purpose and value.",
